Background: The Pocahontas Lift Station Replacement Project is issued by the Okaloosa County Board of County Commissioners in Florida. The project aims to enhance the wastewater management infrastructure by replacing the existing lift station, which is critical for the county's water and sewer services. The goal is to ensure efficient operation and compliance with environmental standards.
Work Details: The project involves site preparation, furnishing, and installation of a corrosion-proof polymer concrete precast wet well using the caisson method with tremie pour for the bottom seal. Key tasks include:

- Clearing and grubbing the site;
- Installing erosion and sedimentation controls;
- Excavating for the wet well shaft;
- Assembling and sealing wet well sections with retainer straps and watertight joints;
- Pouring the tremie seal concrete;
- Installing a secondary pour for the wet well bottom with chamfered edges;
- Conducting buoyancy calculations;
- Performing watertightness testing;
- Backfilling.

Additionally, two (2) ~25 HP submersible, heavy-duty, explosion-proof, non-clog sewer pumps will be furnished and installed along with base elbows, stainless steel discharge piping, guide rail system, pump control panel, and all other appurtenances necessary to complete the work as per attached plans and specifications.
Period of Performance: The contract work is expected to commence upon award and must be completed within a specified timeframe set forth in Article 10 of the Agreement. The exact duration will be defined in accordance with project requirements.
Place of Performance: The project will be performed at the Pocahontas Lift Station site located in Okaloosa County, Florida.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must be certified to conduct business in Florida through the Secretary of State's office. A Certificate of Good Standing from Florida must be provided with bids. Bidders are required to have a valid contractor license as per Chapter 489 of Florida Statutes. Additionally, bidders must comply with insurance requirements as specified in Article 31 of the contract documents.

