Background: Alachua County is undertaking a comprehensive replacement of detention-grade sliding door operating devices at the Alachua County Jail, located at 3333 NE 39th Ave, Gainesville, FL 32609. The project aims to enhance security and functionality within the facility by replacing existing sliding door mechanisms with new, detention-rated sliding device assemblies for various door types throughout the jail. Alachua County has a population of over 250,000 and operates under a Board of five elected County Commissioners.
Work Details: The work includes:
- Removing existing sliding door mechanisms;
- Installing new detention-rated sliding device assemblies for multiple door types including double sliding devices in corridor areas, pod entry sliding devices, and single sliding devices in various housing units;
- Conducting onsite field investigations to verify existing housings, door configurations, clearances, mounting conditions, and mechanical interfaces prior to finalizing submittals or fabrication;
- Demolishing old components;
- Reinstalling and adjusting existing detention doors;
- Applying security caulking;
- Anchoring hardware installation; and
- Performing full operational testing.

All work must maintain facility security at all times, with doors being removed one at a time as they are actively worked on.
Period of Performance: The contract is expected to begin on October 1, 2026, and continue through September 30, 2027. The County has the option to renew this Agreement for three additional one-year periods.
Place of Performance: The work will be performed at the Alachua County Jail located at 3333 NE 39th Ave, Gainesville, FL 32609.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must be qualified and capable of performing the required services while adhering to all applicable laws and industry best practices. They must provide a bid bond equal to at least five percent (5%) of the bid amount. Bidders are required to demonstrate good faith efforts to utilize certified Small Business Enterprises (SBEs) for at least 15% of the dollar value of the bid. Additionally, bidders must comply with Alachua County Government Minimum Wage regulations.

Background: The Florida Department of Environmental Protection is issuing this contract for the Manatee Springs State Park project, titled 'Connect to the Municipalities.' The goal of this contract is to facilitate necessary connections and improvements at the state park, which is vital for environmental management and public access.
