Bidder Requirements: Bidders must be prequalified to submit bids. They can achieve prequalification by providing their Sunbiz and DBPR profiles either prior to or at the time of bid submission. A General Contractor's license may be required based on local permitting agency guidelines.

Background: The Florida Department of Transportation is issuing a contract for roadway improvements along State Road 436 from Lake Howell Road to the Orange County Line in Seminole County. 
The mission of this project is to enhance roadway safety and functionality through various construction activities, including milling, resurfacing, signalization, and sidewalk upgrades. 
The total length of the project is approximately 2.105 miles.
Work Details: The improvements under this contract include: 
- Maintenance of Traffic (MOT) measures such as traffic control officers, special detours for pedestrians or bicycles, arrow boards, portable changeable message signs (PCMS), signalization and maintenance, traffic detection and maintenance, barricades; 
- Protections including sediment barriers and inlets; 
- Earthwork involving excavation; 
- Base course preparation; 
- Asphalt milling and resurfacing; 
- Friction course application; 
- Concrete work for curb and gutter, sidewalks, and ditch pavement; 
- Pavement markings including detectable warnings, painted markings, thermoplastic applications, permanent tape, and raised pavement markers; 
- Signing with various types of signs; 
