- Electrical work including conduit installation and pull/splice boxes; 
- Sod placement. 
Specific quantities include: 240 LF of bridge deck expansion joint rehabilitation with backer rod; 30 CF of polymer nosing for bridge deck expansion joint; 1 LS each for mobilization and maintenance of traffic for two projects; 128 HR for traffic control officers; 21,654 ED for work zone signs; 125,736 ED for channelizing devices; 6,006 ED for arrow boards; 1,356 ED for temporary changeable message signs.
Period of Performance: The contract will be executed over a period of 270 days with an additional 10 days allocated for contract execution. 
A flexible start time is provided with a notice period of 30 days prior to commencement.
Place of Performance: The work will be performed along State Road 436 from Lake Howell Road to the Orange County Line in Seminole County.
Bidder Requirements: Prequalification is required to bid on this contract.

Background: The City of Clermont is soliciting contractors to provide all labor, materials, equipment, and incidentals necessary for the construction of downtown dumpster enclosures. This project aims to enhance the city's waste management infrastructure while ensuring compliance with local regulations and standards.
Work Details: The work includes:
- Installation of temporary erosion and sediment controls;
- Selective demolition and removal of existing curb, sidewalk, asphalt, pavers, and appurtenances;
- Construction of new and modified concrete flatwork including reinforced pads, driveway/approach areas, sidewalk, and ADA ramp tie-ins;
- Curb installation and transitions;
- Brick paver restoration;
- Required utility adjustments/relocations;
- Coordination with utility owners to clear conflicts and maintain services;
- Restoring disturbed areas; and
- Final cleanup.

The project drawings include various sheets detailing the scope of work.
Period of Performance: The performance period will commence upon the issuance of the Purchase Order or Notice To Proceed. It will remain in effect until all services have been completed and accepted by the City's authorized representative.
Place of Performance: The work will be performed in downtown Clermont, Florida.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must possess an active Florida General Contractor License (CGC) or Certified Building Contractor (CBC) license. They must also have a minimum of five years in business under the current name, successful completion of at least three similar projects within the last five years (including one with a value of $150,000 or greater), experience coordinating utility adjustments/relocations, and must maintain a Drug-Free Workplace Program as per Section 287.087, Florida Statutes. Proof of insurance coverage is required.

Background: The Florida Department of Transportation is issuing a contract for roadway maintenance and improvement services in Palm Beach County. The goal of this contract is to implement various improvements through individual Task Work Orders/Work Documents, which will enhance the safety and functionality of roadways in the area.
Work Details: The improvements under this contract include, but are not limited to:

1) Maintenance of Traffic (MOT) including traffic officers, low-profile barriers, free-standing barriers, pedestrian LCDs, arrow boards/panels, crash cushions, PCMS, barricades, and removable tape;

2) Protections such as sediment and inlet protections;

3) Earthwork including excavation and embankment;

4) Concrete work involving removal, gravity walls, curbs, curb/gutters, separators, sidewalks, and driveways;

5) Asphalt work including stabilization, base work, milling, superpave applications, friction courses, and miscellaneous tasks;

6) Pavement markings including patterned markings, detectable markings (RPM), painted markings (thermoplastic), standard refurbishing/removal;

7) Guardrail installation and adjustments;

8) Handrail/guiderail installations;

9) Paver installations;

10) Drainage systems including inlets, manholes, pipe culverts, trench drains;

11) Conduit installations (open trench and directional bore);

12) Pull/splice box installations;

13) Loop assembly installations;

14) Lighting installations including conductors and poles;

15) Signing installations for various types of signs and markers;

16) Utility adjustments such as valve boxes;

17) Electrical work including load centers; and 

18) Sodding throughout Palm Beach County. 

The total award amount for this work-driven contract is $1.5 million over a two-year term.
Period of Performance: The contract will be performed over a period of two years (730 days), with a contract execution period of 10 days.
Place of Performance: The work will be performed throughout Palm Beach County.
Bidder Requirements: Contractors must be pre-qualified to bid on this project. A performance bond is required. Additionally, contractors must provide commercial general liability insurance and workers' compensation insurance as specified in the Standard Specifications for Road and Bridge Construction FY 2025-26.

Background: This fixed contract is for the Broward County Canal Pump Station (S-45) Improvements, issued by the Water Management Division. The project aims to enhance water and wastewater services through the installation of a new drainage pump station, concrete lining of the canal, and restoration of sod areas, ensuring compliance with specified requirements.
Work Details: The scope of work includes:
1. Installation of a new drainage pump station;
2. Concrete lining of the canal;
3. Restoration of sod areas;
4. All ancillary work necessary to complete the project satisfactorily in accordance with the Specifications and Requirements.
Period of Performance: The contract will be performed over a specified period as outlined in the solicitation, with potential for additional quantities up to 20% within one year after award.
Place of Performance: The work will be conducted at the Broward County Canal Pump Station (S-45) location.
Bidder Requirements: Vendors must possess a State of Florida Certified General Contractor license or Broward County General Building Contractor Class 'A' license at the time of submission. Additionally, vendors must perform at least 60% of the total contract price without subcontracting. Compliance with bonding requirements and Florida Department of Environmental Protection Grant Requirements is mandatory.

Background: The Osceola County Board of County Commissioners is seeking proposals from qualified firms to provide design services for the Canoe Creek Road Widening Project. This project aims to enhance transportation infrastructure in Osceola County, which serves as a critical area in Central Florida. The project will widen Canoe Creek Road from a rural 2-lane roadway to a divided, urban 4-lane roadway, addressing the growing transportation needs of the region.
Work Details: The scope of work includes:
- Widening Canoe Creek Road from a rural 2-lane roadway to a divided, urban 4-lane roadway;
- Constructing four (4) signalized intersections;
- Installing street lighting;
- Developing a closed drainage system with ponds;
- Implementing side street improvements.

The project limits extend from Deer Run Road to Pine Tree Drive (Old Canoe Creek Road) over a length of 1.88 miles, including transitions south and north of the intersections. The design must adhere to recommendations from the recently completed Project Development & Environment (PD&E) Study.
Period of Performance: Proposals are due on March 24, 2026.
Place of Performance: The work will be conducted in Osceola County, Florida, specifically along Canoe Creek Road between Deer Run Road and Pine Tree Drive.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must be pre-qualified by the Florida Department of Transportation (FDOT) in Major Highway Design. Proposals must include documentation proving current FDOT prequalification. Additionally, bidders are required to comply with local business tax receipt regulations and provide proof of insurance as stipulated in the solicitation documents.

Background: The Monroe County School District (MCSD) is issuing this Invitation to Bid (ITB) for the procurement of a Small Project General Contractor. The goal of this contract is to provide material and labor for small construction projects necessary to support maintenance operations throughout the district, specifically from Key Largo to Key West. The selected contractor will assist in maintaining and improving school facilities, ensuring they meet safety and operational standards.
Work Details: The contractor will perform small-scale maintenance and construction projects on an as-needed basis, with typical project values under $50,000. Responsibilities include: 
- Providing all labor, materials, tools, and equipment; 
- Maintaining safe working conditions per OSHA standards; 
- Protecting existing structures; 
- Restoring disturbed areas; 
- Providing warranties on workmanship; 
- Coordinating with Maintenance Department staff; 
- Properly managing debris removal. 

Typical project types include wall installation/repair, ceiling installation/repair, door/frame installation/replacement, concrete/masonry work, handrail installation/repair, and storefront/window replacement. Contractors must provide written estimates within three working days of notification and be prepared to mobilize within five days of receiving a purchase order.
Period of Performance: The contract will commence upon award and will continue as needed for small projects throughout the district. Specific timelines for individual task orders will be defined at the time of assignment.
Place of Performance: Work will be performed at various locations within the Monroe County School District, from Key Largo to Key West.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must possess a valid General Contractor License in Florida and comply with all applicable federal, state, and local building codes. They must not be debarred or have had contracts terminated for cause in the past three years. Contractors must ensure that personnel have undergone fingerprinting/background screening if they have direct contact with students or access to school funds. Insurance requirements include: 
- Commercial General Liability ($1 million per incident); 
- Automotive Liability ($1 million combined single limit); 
- Workers' Compensation as mandated by Florida law.

Background: The Central Florida Tourism Oversight District (District) operates a Water Resource Recovery Facility (WRRF) with an annual average daily flow of 20 million gallons per day and a Solid Waste Transfer Station (SWTS) located at South Service Lane, Lake Buena Vista, FL. 
The goal of this contract is to provide vacuum truck cleaning services for these facilities in the South Service Area (SSA).
Work Details: The contractor is required to provide all labor, materials, equipment, and tools necessary for the following services: 
1. Tank cleaning, 
2. Wet well cleaning, 
3. Hydro excavation, 
4. Line jetting cleanout, 
5. Decontamination services related to Sanitary Sewer Spills or Overflows (SSO), and 
6. Environmental cleanup as requested by the District. 

Specific requirements include: 
A. Equipment suitable for removing sewage, grease sediment, and other debris; 
B. Equipment capable of operating in confined spaces; 
C. Equipment for decontamination services related to SSO; 
D. Trained equipment operators; 
E. Compliance with all safety requirements; 
F. Equipment for diagnosing and removing obstructions; 
G. Disposal of contaminated materials off-site with indication of disposal facility in the submittal; 
H. CCTV/Video Inspection as needed. 
All field personnel must have OSHA 10 and OSHA 30 certifications.
Period of Performance: The contract will commence upon receipt of a written Notice-to-Proceed from the Owner and will continue until all work is completed as specified in the contract documents.
Place of Performance: The services will be performed at the Water Resource Recovery Facility and Solid Waste Transfer Station located at South Service Lane, Lake Buena Vista, FL.
Bidder Requirements: Contractors must have OSHA 10 and OSHA 30 certifications for all field personnel working at District facilities.

Background: Williamson County, Texas, is seeking to establish a qualified contractor to upgrade fields 6, 7, 8, and 9 at Southwest Regional Park located at 3005 Co Rd 175, Leander, TX 78641. The project aims to convert four natural grass sports fields into synthetic turf for soccer and football fields. It also includes resurfacing the existing running track. This initiative is managed by the Parks department and is intended to enhance recreational facilities for the community.
Work Details: The scope of work includes:
- Converting four natural grass sports fields (soccer fields 7, 8, 9 and football field 6) to synthetic turf;
- Resurfacing the existing running track around the football field;
- Performing all necessary demolition;
- Conducting earthwork;
- Constructing structural retaining walls;
- Installing utility and drainage infrastructure;
- Modifying the existing irrigation system;
- Making parking modifications;
- Creating accessible walkways to each field;
- Establishing shaded spectator areas;
- Installing permanent security fencing around all fields;
- Revegetation as indicated on the construction plans.

All work must comply with applicable regulations and standards.
Period of Performance: The contractor shall commence work upon instruction from the County and achieve substantial completion within the number of calendar days specified in the Ensuing Agreement. Time extensions may be granted for adverse weather conditions affecting progress.
Place of Performance: The contract will be performed at Southwest Regional Park located at 3005 Co Rd 175, Leander, TX 78641.
Bidder Requirements: Respondents must maintain proper licensing and comply with all federal, state, and local laws related to the services specified in this RFCSP. They are required to provide evidence of experience with similar projects, a list of references from past contracts, and disclose any potential conflicts of interest. Additionally, they must submit a Conflict-of-Interest questionnaire with their proposal.

Background: Miami-Dade County, represented by the Housing and Community Development Department, is seeking proposals from experienced developers for the redevelopment of the Stirrup Plaza Family property. The goal is to design, build, finance, operate, and manage a profitable residential and/or mixed-use development that complies with federal, state, and local requirements. This initiative is subject to approval by the Miami-Dade Board of County Commissioners and the U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD).
Work Details: The selected developer will be responsible for:

1) Redeveloping the Stirrup Plaza Family site into a mixed-use development that includes affordable housing options;

2) Ensuring compliance with all applicable regulations;

3) Engaging in community outreach and involvement during the planning process;

4) Implementing Crime Prevention Through Environmental Design (CPTED) strategies;

5) Providing a detailed project plan that outlines development approach, market viability, project schedule, relevant experience, financial strength, and revenue generation.
Period of Performance: The anticipated timeline for this project includes a proposal evaluation process from April to May 2026, with a projected award date in October 2026.
Place of Performance: The redevelopment will take place at the Stirrup Plaza Family site located in Miami-Dade County, Florida.
Bidder Requirements: Proposers must demonstrate experience in successful residential or mixed-use developments. They are encouraged to engage Section 3 businesses and comply with Davis-Bacon wage requirements. Proposals must include firm commitments for hiring low- and very-low-income individuals as part of their workforce strategy.

Background: The City of Delray Beach, Florida, is seeking bids for the Housing Rehabilitation Program under Case No. 22-101. This initiative aims to enhance housing conditions within the city, specifically targeting properties in need of rehabilitation. 

The program is part of the city's broader mission to improve community living standards and ensure safe, accessible housing for its residents.
Work Details: The selected contractor will be responsible for a variety of rehabilitation tasks at the property located at 4673 Pine Grove Dr., Delray Beach, FL 33445. The specific services required include: 
1) Installation of impact windows; 
2) Replacement of a gliding patio door with a double steel door; 
3) Installation of a one-car garage door; 
4) Installation of base and wall cabinets along with a countertop; 
5) Replacement of the kitchen sink and disposal unit; 
6) Preparation and painting of walls in the room; 
7) Removal of an existing tub and installation of an ADA-compliant shower unit; 
8) Installation of a vanity with sink; 
9) Replacement or installation of medicine cabinets and accessories; 
10) Installation of additional vanity with sink; 
11) Installation of interior light fixtures; and 
12) Replacement or installation of interior doors. 

The contractor must furnish all labor, equipment, and materials necessary for the successful completion of these tasks as per the terms outlined in this Quick Quote solicitation.
Period of Performance: The contract will be awarded as a one-time purchase order. The work is expected to commence following the issuance of a Notice to Proceed by the Neighborhood Services Division, which will occur no later than ten (10) calendar days after contract execution.
Place of Performance: All work will be performed at the property located at 4673 Pine Grove Dr., Delray Beach, FL 33445.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must meet several qualifications to be considered for this contract: They must be registered with the State of Florida to do business, have been in operation for at least five years, possess a Florida State General Contractor’s license or equivalent certification from Palm Beach County, submit acceptable pricing using the provided form, and provide references from previous clients for similar work completed within the last three years. Additionally, bidders must not be listed on any debarment lists and must disclose any conflicts of interest related to City employees.

Background: The City of Clermont is issuing a solicitation for the rehabilitation of an existing StormCapture box inlet structure located on Disston Avenue. The project aims to address roadway depressions caused by displaced bedding material and failure of the interior splash pad, ensuring long-term service and stability of the structure.
Work Details: The work includes:
- Removing and properly disposing of the existing failed interior concrete splash pad;
- Forming and pouring a new 6-foot by 7-foot by 6-inch reinforced concrete splash pad;
- Cleaning, removing, and staging displaced rock for reuse;
- Installing replacement rock to rebuild eroded bedding;
- Repacking and rehabilitating the interior gravel media;
- Removing all debris and waste from the site; and
- Leaving the StormCapture box clean, stable, and fully restored for long-term service.

The project requires confined space entry procedures and appropriate maintenance of traffic (MOT) measures during construction.
Period of Performance: The time of completion/delivery must not exceed sixty (60) calendar days from issuance of the purchase order or notice to proceed.
Place of Performance: The work will be performed at the StormCapture box inlet structure located in the center of Disston Avenue, Clermont, Florida.
Bidder Requirements: All respondents must be registered with the Florida Department of State and licensed to do business in Florida. They must provide proof of insurance as specified in the solicitation, including general liability, automobile liability, and workers' compensation. Respondents are required to submit documentation demonstrating their ability to perform the work, including confined space entry training certifications, FDOT MOT certification for traffic control personnel, applicable contractor licensing information, and references for similar projects completed within the past five years.

Background: The City of Coral Gables Public Works Department is seeking bids for the Street End Improvements Project, aimed at enhancing the street end at Wallace Street, located near the intersection of SW 8th Street and Wallace Street. 

The project is part of the City’s efforts to improve public infrastructure and ensure compliance with the Florida Building Code (FBC) and other applicable regulations.
Work Details: The scope of work includes: 
1) Removal and replacement of the existing sidewalk, including installation of a new ADA mat; 
2) Furnishing and installation of a picket fence and pedestrian gate; 
3) Construction of a new pier/column to support the pedestrian gate; 
4) Furnishing and installation of a street light pole and base, including all associated electrical work; 
5) Replacement of asphalt pavement impacted by construction activities. 

The Contractor must verify all measurements and existing site conditions before submitting pricing.
Period of Performance: The project is expected to be substantially completed within forty-five (45) calendar days from the commencement date stated in the Notice to Proceed, with final completion occurring fifteen (15) calendar days after substantial completion.
Place of Performance: The improvements will take place at Wallace Street, near the intersection with SW 8th Street in Coral Gables, Florida.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must be State of Florida Licensed General Contractors or Miami Dade County Contractors. They must demonstrate three (3) years of experience in providing similar construction services, provide at least three references for similar projects completed in the last three years, hold an active license from the Florida Department of Business and Professional Regulation or a Certificate of Competency from Miami Dade County's Construction Trades Qualifying Board. 

Additionally, bidders must comply with local Occupational License Tax requirements.

Background: The District School Board of Pasco County is issuing this bid to establish a contract for the purchase and installation of a telescopic bleacher seating system at Seven Springs Middle School. The objective is to remove and replace the existing bleacher seating system to ensure public safety. This project aims to enhance the facilities at the school, aligning with the District's mission to provide quality education and safe environments for students.
Work Details: The work under this contract includes:
1) Removal of the existing bleacher seating system;
2) Installation of a new telescopic bleacher seating system;
3) Provision of all necessary labor, materials, equipment, protection, and services required for the replacement;
4) Compliance with safety regulations throughout the project;
5) Submission of professional engineer signed and stamped drawings to the District’s Building Official;
6) Coordination with District’s Construction Services Department for obtaining permits and inspections.
Period of Performance: The anticipated timeline for this project includes a mandatory pre-bid meeting on February 17, 2026, with a response deadline set for March 17, 2026. The work is expected to commence shortly after award notification on April 14, 2026.
Place of Performance: The work will be performed at Seven Springs Middle School located at 2441 Little Road, New Port Richey, FL 34655.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must be licensed contractors in Florida and provide proof of insurance coverage. They are required to submit a current W-9 form, an occupational/business license, and a contractor license issued by the State of Florida. Additionally, bidders must include a plan of execution detailing how they will fulfill the scope of work along with warranty information on products and workmanship.

Background: The Monroe County Board of County Commissioners is seeking proposals for the renovation of the Key West Lighthouse Giftshop. The project aims to enhance the interior of this historic site, which serves as a museum open to the public. The renovations are intended to improve functionality while preserving the building's historical significance.
Work Details: The scope of work includes:
1. Demolition and reconfiguration of interior walls;
2. Demolition of existing tile flooring and replacement with new epoxy flooring;
3. Demolition and replacement of existing plumbing fixtures;
4. Demolition and replacement of existing lighting fixtures;
5. Relocation of existing electrical panels;
6. An additive alternate for the replacement of existing doors, matching the current design.

The contractor is responsible for all labor, materials, tools, permits, and disposal of debris necessary for completing the project as per the provided schematic drawings from Bender & Associates Architects, P.A.
Period of Performance: The anticipated timeline for substantial completion is December 30, 2026, with a Notice to Proceed expected around May 4, 2026.
Place of Performance: The work will be performed at the Key West Lighthouse located at 938 Whitehead Street, Key West, Florida.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must possess all necessary licenses to perform work in Monroe County and provide proof with their proposal. They must also maintain insurance coverage including Employer’s Liability, General Liability, Vehicle Liability, and Architect Errors & Omissions as specified in the proposal documents.

Background: The Hialeah Housing Authority (HHA) is seeking proposals from qualified contractors to provide all necessary materials, labor, and equipment for the re-roofing project at Donald Scott Villas. 
The agency's mission is to provide safe and affordable housing options to the community.
Work Details: The project involves re-roofing at multiple addresses within the Donald Scott Villas, specifically at: 
- 545, 555, 565, 575, 585, 595 West 25 Street; 
- 2535, 2565, 2595 West 6th Avenue; 
- 2590, 2560, 2530, 2535, 2565, 2595 West 5th Way and Court in Hialeah, FL. 
Contractors are required to submit a proposal that includes detailed information about the materials and methods to be used for the roofing work.
Period of Performance: The contract will commence upon award and is expected to be completed within a specified timeframe as determined by the contractor's proposal. 
Proposals are due no later than February 26, 2026.
Place of Performance: The work will be performed at various locations in Hialeah, Florida as specified in the addresses listed above.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must provide a comprehensive proposal including: 
- Company Proposal; 
- Statement for Bidders Qualifications; 
- Non-Collusive Affidavit Form; 
- HUD Form 5370-EZ Contracts Construction; 
- W-9 Form; 
- Section 3 Business Self-Certification Form; 
- Certification Regarding Debarment; 
- Acknowledgement of Davis Bacon Wage Rate; 
- List of Subcontractor/Material Supplier Forms; 
- Copy of Licenses; and any signed Addenda. 
All documents must be properly executed and notarized.

Background: The Florida Department of Environmental Protection is issuing this addendum for the Manatee Springs State Park project, identified as DEP BID NO. BDC18-25/26. The purpose of the contract is to connect the park to local municipalities, ensuring proper infrastructure and environmental compliance.
Work Details: The contract includes the incorporation of a septic report, permits, and revised plans into the bid package. Key revisions for the Assistant Park Manager’s Residence include:

1. Additional demolition of a 13" DBH tree (Sheet C110);
2. Addition of 10 LF of sediment control fence (Sheet C110);
3. Drain field sizing revisions (Sheets C111 and C112);
4. Grading revisions (Sheet C113).

The revised bid package can be accessed online at the provided link.
Period of Performance: The specific period of performance is not detailed in the addendum; however, it is expected that work will commence following bid acceptance.
Place of Performance: The work will be performed at Manatee Springs State Park, located in Florida.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must sign this addendum to acknowledge receipt and include it with their bid submission to avoid rejection. There are no specific set-aside certifications or local requirements mentioned.

Background: The Broward County Facilities Management Division (FMD) is seeking a qualified firm to provide comprehensive roofing and waterproofing consultant services. The goal of this contract is to assess and improve the condition of County facilities, focusing on building envelopes including roofs, walls, storefronts, doors, and window systems. The services aim to ensure the longevity and functionality of these structures in alignment with the County's mission.
Work Details: The consultant will provide a range of services including:

1) Inventory and assessment of building structures;
2) Identification of repair needs;
3) Development of specifications for roofing and waterproofing projects;
4) Solicitation assistance;
5) Construction administration;
6) Monitoring services as applicable.

Specific tasks include reviewing and updating specifications organized per the Construction Specifications Institute's Master Format, developing material and installation specifications, providing detail drawings, defining contractor qualifications, conducting inventories of roofs and exterior elevations, performing inspections to document conditions, developing construction documents for procurement processes, providing project administration services during construction phases, and offering additional services such as aerial infrared inspections and electronic leak detection.
Period of Performance: The contract will be executed over a defined period with individual projects requiring specific work authorizations that outline project-specific scopes of work, schedules, and cost breakdowns.
Place of Performance: Services will be performed at various County facilities located within Broward County.
Bidder Requirements: Vendors must possess a valid Florida state license as either a Licensed Professional Architect or Licensed Professional Engineer at the time of submittal. Additionally, vendors must comply with Broward County’s Criminal History Screening Practices Ordinance and submit required certifications related to lobbyist registration. Vendors are encouraged to submit all requested information electronically through Bonfire BPRO by the specified deadline.

Background: This solicitation is issued by the Broward County Parks and Recreation Division, which manages approximately 50 regional parks and nature centers, neighborhood parks, and other County properties. The goal of this contract is to provide on-demand construction and improvements to these parks and properties, ensuring compliance with all applicable building codes, including Florida Building Code (FBC) High Velocity Hurricane Zone (HVHZ) requirements.
Work Details: The contractor will furnish all labor, materials, equipment, supervision, and incidentals necessary for the construction, improvement, and renovation of County parks. The scope includes:

1. New vertical construction such as restrooms, shades, and shelters;
2. Underground utilities including electric, drainage, water, and sewer;
3. New athletic courts with surfacing;
4. Paved parking lots and minor roads;
5. Minor landscaping and irrigation;
6. Site development and rehydration;
7. Sidewalks and trails;
8. Site lighting.

Excluded from this contract are vertical demolition; building renovations or repairs; playgrounds; sea walls; pre-engineered buildings; resurfacing of athletic courts; and boardwalks.
Period of Performance: The initial contract period shall commence upon award and will last for two years. The Director of Purchasing may renew the contract for two additional one-year periods based on vendor performance.
Place of Performance: Work will be performed at various County parks and properties throughout Broward County.
Bidder Requirements: Vendors must possess a State of Florida license as a Certified General Contractor or Certified Building Contractor or a Broward County General Building Contractor Class 'A' or 'B'. Vendors must also comply with the Broward County Business Enterprise (CBE) Goal Participation of 25%. Additionally, vendors must provide proof of qualifications within three business days upon request.

Background: The City of Homestead Public Works and Engineering/Streets & Stormwater Department is seeking to retain a qualified contractor to provide materials, equipment, and labor for the installation and repair of a fence at the vacant lot adjacent to 3275 Park of Commerce Blvd. 
The goal is to ensure that the new fence installation meets current federal, state, and local standards for roadside safety and compliance.
Work Details: The contractor shall provide all labor, equipment, and materials necessary to complete the following tasks: 
- Install 537 linear feet of new commercial (9 gauge) chain link fence at 84” in height, including terminal and line posts and top rail; 
- Repair damaged chain link fence fronting Park of Commerce; 
- Install new rolling hardware on two existing rolling gates; 
- Repair rolling gate track; 
- Install three strands of 12.5-gauge barb wire over approximately 537 linear feet. 
Mobilization costs must be included for personnel, equipment, and materials. All work must comply with applicable FDOT, MUTCD, and local standards. The contractor is responsible for obtaining all necessary permits from Development Services and ensuring compliance with permitting requirements. Clear before-and-after photo documentation of the work area is required.
Period of Performance: The project is expected to commence after the mandatory site visit on January 21, 2026, with completion deadlines aligned with the City's schedule.
Place of Performance: Vacant Lot adjacent to 3275 Park of Commerce Blvd., Homestead, FL 33030.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must possess a valid occupational/business license and state registration in Florida. They must not be listed as an excluded party in SAM (System for Award Management). Insurance certificates indicating satisfactory coverage are required prior to contract execution. Bidders must also comply with E-Verify requirements for employee work authorization verification.

Background: The School Board of Lee County, Florida, is seeking qualifications for Construction Management Services for the HVAC Renovation project at Success Academy. The goal of this contract is to engage a Construction Manager who will work collaboratively with the School Board’s Facility Development & Programming Department and a selected Mechanical, Electrical, and Plumbing (MEP) Firm. 

The target total project cost is estimated between $8 million and $12 million, which encompasses design, construction, labor, materials, and other related expenses.
Work Details: The awarded Construction Manager will be responsible for: 
- Assisting during the preliminary design phase; 
- Overseeing design development; 
- Managing the construction document phase; 
- Scheduling and coordination of all project activities; 
- Ensuring timely and economical completion of the project. 

The Construction Manager will also handle all aspects of construction management including compliance with applicable codes and regulations.
Period of Performance: The contract will commence upon award and is expected to continue until the successful completion of the HVAC renovation project. The anticipated timeline for submission of electronic qualification statements is by 2:00 PM EST on February 18, 2026.
Place of Performance: The work will be performed at Success Academy located in Lee County, Florida.
Bidder Requirements: Respondents must attend a mandatory pre-submission meeting and site walkthrough scheduled for January 28, 2026. Additionally, bidders must comply with specific licensing requirements as outlined in Florida Statutes regarding public entity crimes. Companies must not be on the Scrutinized Companies that Boycott Israel List or engaged in any boycott against Israel.

Background: The School Board of Lee County, Florida, is seeking qualifications for Construction Management Services for the HVAC Renovation project at Mariner High School. The goal of this contract is to ensure the successful, timely, and economical completion of the project, which is expected to cost between $8 million and $12 million. 

The selected Construction Manager will collaborate with the School Board’s Facility Development & Programming Department and a Mechanical, Electrical and Plumbing (MEP) Firm throughout various phases of the project.
Work Details: The awarded Construction Manager will be responsible for: 
- Assisting during the preliminary design phase; 
- Overseeing design development; 
- Managing the construction document phase; 
- Scheduling and coordination; 
- Ensuring compliance with safety regulations; 
- Maintaining good discipline on site; 
- Providing all necessary labor, materials, equipment, and utilities for project execution; 
- Ensuring that all work complies with applicable laws and safety standards. 

Additionally, the Construction Manager must develop a safety plan for the project and ensure that all personnel are trained in safety measures.
Period of Performance: The contract will commence upon Board approval and is expected to last until the completion of the HVAC renovation project. The anticipated timeline includes a mandatory pre-submission meeting on January 29, 2026, with responses due by February 18, 2026.
Place of Performance: The work will be performed at Mariner High School located in Cape Coral, Florida.
Bidder Requirements: Respondents must comply with specific requirements including: 
- Attendance at a mandatory pre-submission meeting; 
- Submission of electronic qualification statements via the Bonfire Platform by the specified deadline; 
- Possession of necessary licenses and insurance as required by Florida law; 
- Adherence to public entity crime statutes; 
- Certification that they are not on any scrutinized companies list related to boycotting Israel.

Background: The School Board of Lee County is seeking qualifications for Construction Management Services for the HVAC Renovation at Estero High School. The goal of this contract is to ensure the successful, timely, and economical completion of the project, which has a target total cost between $8 million and $12 million, including design, construction, labor, and materials.

The selected Construction Manager will work closely with the School Board’s Facility Development & Programming Department and the chosen Mechanical, Electrical, and Plumbing (MEP) Firm.
Work Details: The awarded Construction Manager will be responsible for:
- Assisting during the preliminary design phase;
- Overseeing design development;
- Managing the construction document phase;
- Scheduling and coordination of all activities related to the project;
- Ensuring compliance with all applicable codes and regulations;
- Maintaining safety on site; and
- Managing all personnel involved in the project.

The Construction Manager must also ensure that all materials and services provided meet specifications and are delivered in new condition.
Period of Performance: The contract is expected to commence upon Board approval and will continue until the completion of the HVAC renovation project. The submission deadline for electronic qualification responses is set for 2:00 PM EST on February 18, 2026.
Place of Performance: The work will be performed at Estero High School located at 21900 River Ranch Rd., Estero, FL 33928.
Bidder Requirements: Respondents must attend a mandatory pre-submission conference scheduled for January 30, 2026. They must also comply with Florida Statutes regarding public entity crimes and provide proof of Workers’ Compensation Insurance. Additionally, bidders must not be listed on any Scrutinized Companies List or engage in a boycott of Israel.

Background: Broward County, Florida, through its Facilities Management Division (FMD), is seeking a qualified firm to provide Roofing and Waterproofing Consultant Services. The goal of this contract is to update and maintain a proactive program for capital planning, preventive and corrective maintenance of the building envelope for all County facilities, which includes roofing, wall, entrance, and window systems.
Work Details: The consultant will provide comprehensive services related to roofing and waterproofing assessments and improvements. Specific tasks include:
- Inventorying and assessing building structures;
- Identifying repair needs;
- Developing specifications;
- Providing solicitation assistance;
- Conducting construction administration;
- Monitoring services;
- Reviewing and updating specifications for roofing or waterproofing solicitations;
- Conducting inventories of roofs and exterior elevations;
- Performing inspections to document existing conditions;
- Developing construction documents for roof replacement or extensive repairs;
- Assisting with project administration services during construction;
- Providing additional services such as aerial infrared inspections and electronic leak detection.
Period of Performance: The contract duration is open-ended with an initial term of two years, followed by three one-year renewal options.
Place of Performance: Services will be performed at various County facilities located in Broward County, Florida.
Bidder Requirements: Vendors must possess a State of Florida Licensed Professional Architect or Licensed Professional Engineer at the time of submittal. Additionally, vendors must comply with Broward County’s Criminal History Screening Practices Ordinance and submit the required certifications including Domestic Partnership Act Certification as a tiebreaker criterion. Vendors are also required to submit financial statements demonstrating financial capability.

Background: The DeSoto County Board of County Commissioners (BOCC) is seeking Professional Engineering Services from qualified professional engineers registered in the State of Florida. DeSoto County has obtained grant funding for three individual road improvement projects through the Small County Outreach Program (SCOP) and Small County Road Assistance Program (SCRAP). 

The goal is to select one RFQ Respondent to award Construction Engineering and Inspection (CEI) contracts for these projects, which include NE Cubitis Avenue, SE Hargrave Avenue, and SW Liverpool Road. The design of all projects is complete, and construction letting will occur concurrently with the advertisement of the RFQ for CEI services or shortly thereafter. Separate construction bids will be released for each project, with a construction notice to proceed anticipated as early as Spring 2026.
Work Details: The CEI services required include: 
- Attendance at the Construction Kick-Off Meeting; 
- Conducting regular progress meetings on a weekly basis; 
- Providing an engineer's summary letter monthly; 
- Field inspections by a qualified construction inspector; 
- Periodic field visits by a Florida Registered Professional Engineer; 
- Review and approval of Proctor/LBR reports and density test reports; 
- Review of all submittals and shop drawings from contractors; 
- Responding to Contractor Requests for Information (RFI); 
- Reviewing Change Order Requests and Applications for Payment; 
- Attending walk-throughs for Substantial and Final Completion; 
- Issuing Certificates of Substantial and Final Completion; 
- Signing the Engineer's Certification of Compliance on the Notice of Completion; 
- Other necessary CEI responsibilities. 

The anticipated CEI budget is $370,000 across three projects with total anticipated construction costs of $4,080,000.
Period of Performance: The anticipated schedule for the CEI solicitation includes releasing the RFQ in January 2026, with responses due in February 2026. Selection Committee evaluations and interviews will occur in March 2026, followed by contract negotiations and BOCC approval in March 2026. The construction kick-off is expected in March/April 2026.
Place of Performance: The projects are located in DeSoto County, Florida, specifically along NE Cubitis Avenue (3.83 miles), SE Hargrave Avenue (0.99 miles), and SW Liverpool Road.
Bidder Requirements: Respondents must be qualified professional engineers registered in Florida. They should include services from a Florida licensed laboratory and testing firm either in-house or subcontracted. There are no specific set-aside certifications mentioned.

Background: The City of Boca Raton, Florida is issuing a solicitation for the Transfer Pumping Upgrades at the Water Treatment Plant. The goal of this contract is to enhance the operational efficiency and structural integrity of the Water Treatment Plant's Transfer Pumping Station, aligning with the city's commitment to providing high-quality water services to its residents.
Work Details: The project involves furnishing all labor, materials, equipment, services, and incidentals necessary for upgrades at the Water Treatment Plant's Transfer Pumping Station. Specific tasks include:

- Modifications and enhancements to the building’s architecture;
- Structural strengthening;
- Modifications to the existing process mechanical system;
- Upgrades to mechanical and electrical equipment inside the building;
- Miscellaneous site improvements encompassing civil, mechanical, electrical work, and all incidentals required to complete the project in accordance with the Contract Documents.
Place of Performance: The work will be performed at the Utility Department located at 1401 Glades Road, Boca Raton, Florida.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders are required to submit sealed bids along with original bid security directly to the City of Boca Raton. There are no specific set-aside certifications or local requirements mentioned in the solicitation.

Background: The City of Fort Lauderdale, Florida, is seeking bids from qualified contractors to provide construction services for the Galt Ocean Mile Beautification Project. This project aims to enhance the infrastructure and aesthetics of the area, aligning with the city's mission to improve public spaces and promote community engagement.
Work Details: The work to be accomplished under this contract includes:
- Milling and resurfacing of roadway;
- Construction of bike lanes;
- Widening of sidewalks;
- Relocation of existing trees;
- Addition of landscape materials;
- Installation of new street fixtures;
- Creation of unloading areas;
- Construction of raised table crosswalks or intersections.

The project will adhere to the FDOT Standard Specifications for Road and Bridge Construction FY 2023-24 and other applicable local agency program specifications.
Period of Performance: The contract will be performed over a specified period, with exact dates to be determined upon award. The bids are due electronically by February 17, 2026.
Place of Performance: The geographic location for this contract is Galt Ocean Mile in the City of Fort Lauderdale, Florida.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must possess a Certified General Contractor (CGC) license or any other State or County licenses deemed legally permissible by the City. Additionally, any subcontractors employed must also be licensed and insured. A bid security in the form of a certified check, cashier's check, bank officer's check, or bid bond for five percent (5%) of the bid amount is required. Bidders must comply with local business preference requirements if applicable.

Background: The Village of Royal Palm Beach, Florida is issuing this Invitation to Bid for the Veterans Park Demolition project. The goal of this contract is to demolish existing structures and repurpose the area to enhance the park's landscape, aligning with the village's mission to maintain and improve public spaces for community use.
Work Details: The scope of work includes:
1. Demolition of the existing splash pad;
2. Removal of underground vaults;
3. Dismantling of electrical panels;
4. Repurposing the area with new landscaping and irrigation systems;
5. Restoration of select concrete statues within the park.
Period of Performance: The contract work is expected to be performed following the bid opening on January 14, 2026, with specific timelines to be determined post-award.
Place of Performance: The work will be performed at Veterans Park, located at 1036 Royal Palm Beach, FL 33411.
Bidder Requirements: Bids must include a Bid Security in the form of a certified bank check or a Bid Bond, amounting to no less than five percent of the total bid price. Additionally, bidders must not be on the convicted vendor list as per F.S. 287.133 (2) (a), which prohibits individuals or affiliates from contracting with public entities for a period of 36 months.

Background: The Central Florida Tourism Oversight District (CFTOD) is seeking a qualified contractor to replace both AMIL gates at Water Control Structure S-405A. This structure, a Waterman Industries Model C-12 Constant Upstream Level Gate, has been in continuous use since its construction in the late 1960s. The goal of this contract is to ensure the functionality and safety of the water control structure through necessary repairs and replacements.
Work Details: The contractor will replace both AMIL gates in kind and perform minimal repairs on the concrete portions of the water control structure to create a watertight seal. Specific tasks include:

1) Removal of bearing housing units from existing gates for CFTOD Planning & Engineering;
2) Replacement of the eastern safety chain post;
3) Realignment of the bent ladder safety handrail;
4) Installation of new AMIL gates, with shop drawings submitted for approval prior to ordering;
5) Use of Waterman Industries as the approved vendor for gate replacement;
6) Disposal of existing ballast material and installation of new ballast (rebar or lead);
7) Preparation and submission of a Storm Water Pollution Prevention Plan (SWPPP);
8) Installation of non-erosive cofferdams and dewatering systems;
9) Restoration of site post-completion, including stabilization of canal slopes;
10) Compliance with all safety regulations and guidelines throughout the project.
Period of Performance: The project is anticipated to commence with a Notice to Proceed on March 11, 2026, and must be completed no later than November 11, 2026, totaling approximately eight months.
Place of Performance: The work will be performed at Water Control Structure S-405A located within the jurisdiction of the Central Florida Tourism Oversight District.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must hold a General Contractor License and have at least eight years of marine construction experience. A primary contact/project manager with similar experience is required. Contractors must also have an Advanced Temporary Traffic Control (TTC/MOT) certification and a Certified FDEP Erosion Control Inspector on staff. Experience with water control structures is preferred. A performance and payment bond is required if bids exceed $200,000.

Background: The Central Florida Tourism Oversight District (CFTOD) is seeking a qualified contractor to replace both AMIL Gates at Water Control Structure S-405A. This structure, which has been in continuous use since its construction in the late 1960s, plays a crucial role in water control within the district. The goal of this contract is to ensure the functionality and integrity of the water control structure by replacing the gates and performing necessary repairs.
Work Details: The contractor will be responsible for replacing both AMIL Gates at Water Control Structure S-405A in kind. The work includes:
1) Performing minimal repairs on the concrete portions of the structure to create a watertight seal;
2) Removing bearing housing units from the existing gate and providing them to CFTOD Planning & Engineering before the gates are removed off-site for disposal;
3) Replacing the existing eastern safety chain post;
4) Realigning the bent ladder safety handrail.

The structure features a dual AMIL Gate System with an upstream control elevation of 96.00-ft and is a Waterman Industries Model C-12 Constant Upstream Level Gate with a maximum gate opening of 2’-0.84”.
Place of Performance: The work will be performed at Water Control Structure S-405A, located within the jurisdiction of the Central Florida Tourism Oversight District.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must register on the PlanetBids platform to participate in this solicitation. There are preferences for local vendors, veteran small businesses, and opportunity zone businesses on most solicitations.

Background: The Florida Department of Transportation is issuing this contract for the construction of a pedestrian bridge, milling and resurfacing, drainage, sidewalk, fencing, lighting, and signing and marking at Fort Fraser Trail over SR 60 in Polk County. 

The project aims to enhance transportation infrastructure and improve safety for pedestrians.
Work Details: The improvements under this contract consist of: 
- Construction of a pedestrian bridge; 
- Milling and resurfacing of existing pavement; 
- Installation of drainage systems; 
- Construction of sidewalks; 
- Installation of fencing; 
- Installation of lighting; 
- Signing and marking. 

Specific items include various classes of concrete (Class NS, Class II, Class IV), reinforcing steel for the bridge superstructure and substructure, prestressed concrete beams, preformed pile holes, driven piles, traffic control devices, and various types of signage.
Period of Performance: The contract will be performed over a period of 375 days with an execution period of 10 days. The flexible start time is set at 60 days from the acquisition date.
Place of Performance: The work will be performed at Fort Fraser Trail over SR 60 in Polk County, Florida.
Bidder Requirements: Contractors must have a current certificate of qualification as per Florida Statute 337.14(1) for projects exceeding $250,000.00. Bidders must also submit a proposal guaranty of 5% for bids over $150,000.00. Additionally, contractors must be prequalified in at least 50% of the project scope.
